course: dictionary
lesson: 5774
title: One word, two worlds
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word lunula is one of them. Its meaning depends on the subject you are studying, so the context tells you which meaning you need. «The white half-moon at the base of a nail, the lunula, is part of the nail root and is often biggest on the thumbs.» Here the words nail and thumbs are the clues, so this is the science meaning.
explain: In history, the same word names an object. A lunula can also be a flat gold neck ornament shaped like a crescent moon, made in Ireland and Britain in the Bronze Age. If you read about old gold in a museum, the clues will be words like Bronze Age, gold and ornament. Always ask: which subject is this text about?
explain: Check your choice by swapping the meaning into the sentence. If the sentence still makes sense with your meaning, you have probably chosen well. If it does not, go back to the clues and try the other meaning.
fact: A lunula is a white half-moon shape at the base of a fingernail or toenail.
fact: The lunula is part of the nail root, and it is often biggest on the thumbs.
fact: A lunula can also be a flat gold neck ornament shaped like a crescent moon.
fact: Gold lunulae were made in Ireland and Britain in the Bronze Age, and museums such as the National Museum of Ireland show them.
fact: Lunula is a noun, and its plural is lunulae.
exercise: «The white half-moon at the base of a nail, the lunula, is part of the nail root.» Where is the lunula? | On the palm of the hand | Inside the thumb | *At the base of a nail | On the tip of the fingernail
exercise: In a history lesson about the Bronze Age, what is a gold lunula? | A type of Bronze Age sword | *A flat gold neck ornament shaped like a crescent moon | A coin used for buying food | A small bird found in Ireland
exercise: Find and copy the words that show the science meaning in «The lunula is often biggest on the thumbs.» | museum | *nail | Bronze Age | gold
test: «A gold lunula was found in a Bronze Age grave.» What does gold lunula most likely mean? | A gold ring for a finger | A gold coin used for trade | A gold bowl for food | *A crescent-shaped gold neck ornament
test: Which statement about the lunula on a nail is true? | It is biggest on the little finger | It is a kind of bone in the hand | *It is often biggest on the thumbs | It is found on the ear
exam: Which two meanings does lunula have, one from science and one from history? | A small bone in the wrist, and a Bronze Age sword | *A white half-moon at the base of a nail, and a flat gold neck ornament shaped like a crescent moon | A type of nail polish, and a museum in Ireland | A crescent moon in the sky, and a gold coin
